Align stream reset, stop, credit and direct-receive handling with RFC 9000.

Applies to picoquic 70b5fd5aafdd2d6c349ff783202ece9d778bcaf2, after 0001 and
0002.

Eight related topics, retaining the existing regression coverage:

- Reset after FIN. Upstream PR2279 already uses sent_offset and permits reset
  in the "Data Sent" state (RFC 9000 Section 3.1); that correction is no
  longer supplied here. Retain the stricter ALREADY_CLOSED refusal once the
  sent bytes and FIN are acknowledged, context preservation on refusal, and
  idempotent repeated reset. Clear the context only on an accepted reset.
- Reset prefix retirement. A reset stream retires only once its reset and its
  reliable prefix are both acknowledged (picoquic_is_stream_acked), and the
  acknowledgement of a RESET_STREAM_AT retires it through that rule.
- Reliable Size check. A received RESET_STREAM_AT whose Reliable Size exceeds
  its Final Size closes the connection with FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR
  (draft-ietf-quic-reliable-stream-reset Section 4).
- Prefix delivery. The chunk that completes the reliable prefix of a received
  RESET_STREAM_AT is delivered before the reset is signalled; nothing is
  delivered on that stream once the reset is signalled.
- Empty STREAM frame ACK. An ACK of an empty non-FIN STREAM frame records
  nothing, instead of underflowing to a range covering the whole stream.
- Stream credit at final size. MAX_STREAMS for a peer-initiated stream is
  replenished once its receive half is complete: the FIN check runs after the
  final size is stored, a reset is complete once its reliable prefix is
  consumed, and duplicate terminals are counted once. That timing is this
  provider's policy; RFC 9000 Section 4.6 does not fix it.
- Reset and stop direction. A reset needs a sending part (Section 19.4) and a
  stop a receiving part (Section 19.5); otherwise
  PICOQUIC_ERROR_INVALID_STREAM_ID, refused before the stream or its context
  changes.
- Direct-receive lifetime. A stream handed over to direct receive is not
  retired from inside the data callback: its close check is queued
  (picoquic_queue_stream_close_check) and runs at the next packet
  preparation.

The upstream reset_at_end acknowledged-FIN row expects the retained
ALREADY_CLOSED refusal and checks context preservation without preventing
its later reliable-size cases from running.

Tests (picoquic_ct): reset_at_end, stream_reset_after_fin, reset_after_fin_wire,
stream_reset_prefix_retirement, reset_stream_at_reliable_size,
stream_reset_at_prefix_delivery, stream_empty_frame_ack,
empty_stream_frame_ack_wire, stream_credit_receive_complete,
stream_reset_stop_direction, stop_sending_local_unidir,
stream_direct_receive_handover and direct_receive_close_check. In LibMoQ:
adapters/picoquic/tests/test_pq_reset_after_fin.c and
test_pq_provider_stream_credit.c.

